<title>UK: KfW mandates Dresdner, Merrill for 10-yr mark bond.</title>
<headline>KfW mandates Dresdner, Merrill for 10-yr mark bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kreditanstalt fuer Wiederaufbau (KfW) plans to issue a 10-year mark benchmark bond and has mandated Dresdner Kleinwort Benson and Merrill Lynch as joint bookrunners, Dresdner said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to be launched early next week depending on market conditions, the statement said.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
<p>KfW is a regular Euromarket borrower. Its last sizeable deal was a $500 million 10-year bond issued on February 19. It was priced to yield 20 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
